1
00:00:01,207 --> 00:00:04,004
♫ In the not too distant future

2
00:00:04,004 --> 00:00:07,537
♫ Somewhere in time and space

3
00:00:07,537 --> 00:00:10,594
♫ Mike Nelson and his robot pals

4
00:00:10,594 --> 00:00:13,865
♫ Are caught in an endless chase

5
00:00:13,865 --> 00:00:16,757
♫ Pursued by a woman whose name is Pearl

6
00:00:16,757 --> 00:00:20,041
♫ An evil gal who wants to rule the world

7
00:00:20,041 --> 00:00:22,862
♫ She threw a few things in her purse

8
00:00:22,862 --> 00:00:24,740
♫ And in her rocket ship she hunts

9
00:00:24,740 --> 00:00:29,708
♫ Him all across the universe.
♫ I'll get you!

10
00:00:29,708 --> 00:00:32,139
♫ I'll send him cheesy movies

11
00:00:32,139 --> 00:00:35,907
♫ The worst I can find
♫ la-la-la

12
00:00:35,907 --> 00:00:38,613
♫ He'll have to sit and watch them all

13
00:00:38,613 --> 00:00:41,497
♫ And I'll monitor his mind
♫ la-la-la

14
00:00:41,497 --> 00:00:44,851
♫ Now keep in mind Mike can't control

15
00:00:44,851 --> 00:00:46,699
♫ Where the movies begin or end

16
00:00:46,699 --> 00:00:47,532
♫ la-la-la

17
00:00:47,532 --> 00:00:50,934
♫ He'll try to keep his sanity

18
00:00:50,934 --> 00:00:55,101
♫ With the help of his robot friends.

19
00:00:56,085 --> 00:00:58,114
♫ Robot Roll Call:

20
00:00:58,114 --> 00:00:59,634
♫ Cambot!
♫ You're on!

21
00:00:59,634 --> 00:01:00,972
♫ Gypsy!
♫ Oh, my stars!

22
00:01:00,972 --> 00:01:02,354
♫ Tom Servo!
♫ Check me out!

23
00:01:02,354 --> 00:01:03,187
♫ Croooow!
♫ I'm different!

24
00:01:03,187 --> 00:01:06,802
♫ If you're wondering
how he eats and breathes

25
00:01:06,802 --> 00:01:10,290
♫ And other science facts
♫ la-la-la

26
00:01:10,290 --> 00:01:11,773
♫ Just repeat to yourself

27
00:01:11,773 --> 00:01:15,590
♫ It's just a show, I
should really just relax

28
00:01:15,590 --> 00:01:19,757
♫ For Mystery Science Theater 3000 ♫

29
00:01:20,906 --> 00:01:24,302
(guitar strum)

30
00:01:24,302 --> 00:01:25,970
(metal door slamming)
(squeaking metal)

31
00:01:25,970 --> 00:01:27,500
(metal door slamming)

32
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:28,415
(computer beep)

33
00:01:28,415 --> 00:01:31,022
(metal door slamming)

34
00:01:31,022 --> 00:01:32,256
(door slamming)

35
00:01:32,256 --> 00:01:33,856
(squeaking metal door shutting)

36
00:01:33,856 --> 00:01:34,689
(metal door slamming)

37
00:01:34,689 --> 00:01:35,911
(squeaking metal)

38
00:01:35,911 --> 00:01:38,369
- [Voiceover] Ladies and Gypsy,

39
00:01:38,369 --> 00:01:42,186
Michael Nelson is Lord of the Dance.

40
00:01:42,186 --> 00:01:43,019
- Oh!

41
00:01:43,920 --> 00:01:45,342
Did the other one die?

42
00:01:45,342 --> 00:01:46,175
- Um, no.

43
00:01:46,175 --> 00:01:50,342
Anyway, Michael Nelson
is Lord of the Dance.

44
00:01:50,342 --> 00:01:51,300
- Oh, okay.

45
00:01:51,300 --> 00:01:52,133
- [Tom] Three, four.

46
00:01:52,133 --> 00:01:52,966
- [Crow And Tom] (singing while tapping)

47
00:01:52,966 --> 00:01:57,133
♫ Dadadada dadadada dadadada dadadada ♫

48
00:02:00,077 --> 00:02:01,244
- Oh, um, yay.

49
00:02:04,972 --> 00:02:08,301
Well, there's this sink
I need to take a look at,

50
00:02:08,301 --> 00:02:09,134
so I'll just--
- [Tom] Three, four.

51
00:02:09,134 --> 00:02:09,967
- [Crow And Tom] (singing while tapping)

52
00:02:09,967 --> 00:02:10,800
♫ Dadadada dadadada
dadadada dadadada dadadada ♫

53
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:12,217
- Oh! Your Honor.

54
00:02:16,605 --> 00:02:17,438
- [Mike] Ah.

55
00:02:17,438 --> 00:02:18,355
- Oh, okay.

56
00:02:20,262 --> 00:02:21,678
We'll be right back.
- [Tom] Three, four.

57
00:02:21,678 --> 00:02:22,511
- [Crow And Tom] (singing while tapping)

58
00:02:22,511 --> 00:02:24,336
♫ Dadadada dadadada
dadadada dadadada dadadada ♫

59
00:02:24,336 --> 00:02:25,348
- Oh.

60
00:02:25,348 --> 00:02:28,181
(high-tech music)

61
00:02:32,046 --> 00:02:33,544
(Mike inhales and exhales)

62
00:02:33,544 --> 00:02:35,794
- Um, Mike, it's over, huh?

63
00:02:36,732 --> 00:02:39,489
- [Tom] Hey, Lord of the Pants,
can you tear yourself away

64
00:02:39,489 --> 00:02:40,362
from yourself for a minute?

65
00:02:40,362 --> 00:02:42,556
We got someone calling from the planet.

66
00:02:42,556 --> 00:02:43,389
- Hello.

67
00:02:44,351 --> 00:02:45,309
- Oh, hello, Mike.

68
00:02:45,309 --> 00:02:46,689
- I should say, hello Mike.

69
00:02:46,689 --> 00:02:47,522
Hello--
- I don't think so.

70
00:02:47,522 --> 00:02:48,355
Hello, Mike.
- Hello, Mike.

71
00:02:48,355 --> 00:02:51,843
- Hello, Mike.
(arguing)

72
00:02:51,843 --> 00:02:54,059
- Hey, what the Sam Hill is going on?

73
00:02:54,059 --> 00:02:54,892
Where's Mrs. F?

74
00:02:54,892 --> 00:02:55,725
- Pain--

75
00:02:57,495 --> 00:02:59,250
- Do you mind terribly if I explain?

76
00:02:59,250 --> 00:03:00,083
- No, be my guest.

77
00:03:00,083 --> 00:03:01,274
You're not in charge.

78
00:03:01,274 --> 00:03:02,116
Not in charge.

79
00:03:02,116 --> 00:03:02,949
- Die.

80
00:03:02,949 --> 00:03:06,118
Mike, Pearl is driving those
horrid little children home

81
00:03:06,118 --> 00:03:09,279
and Bobo here who, by the
way, is not at all smelly

82
00:03:09,279 --> 00:03:12,629
or riddled with infection,
simply cannot accept the fact

83
00:03:12,629 --> 00:03:13,918
that I am in charge.

84
00:03:13,918 --> 00:03:14,751
- You are not.

85
00:03:14,751 --> 00:03:15,919
- I am, too.

86
00:03:15,919 --> 00:03:16,817
Read the note.

87
00:03:16,817 --> 00:03:18,155
- What is it?

88
00:03:18,155 --> 00:03:20,505
(making noises as he reads)

89
00:03:20,505 --> 00:03:23,263
- It says, while I'm away,
the Brain Guy is in charge.

90
00:03:23,263 --> 00:03:26,013
- It does not, give me that note.

91
00:03:27,117 --> 00:03:30,721
(making noises as he reads)

92
00:03:30,721 --> 00:03:32,630
It says you're a dodo head.

93
00:03:32,630 --> 00:03:33,889
- I'm dodo head?

94
00:03:33,889 --> 00:03:35,528
Of all the mitigated gall.

95
00:03:35,528 --> 00:03:37,036
You're the dodo head.
- You're the dodo head.

96
00:03:37,036 --> 00:03:37,927
- No, you're the dodo head.

97
00:03:37,927 --> 00:03:38,927
- Dodo, dodo

98
00:03:40,307 --> 00:03:42,478
- Hey, hey, hey, not
that I care, but you guys

99
00:03:42,478 --> 00:03:44,304
are gonna have to figure
out how to get along

100
00:03:44,304 --> 00:03:45,960
until she gets back.

101
00:03:45,960 --> 00:03:48,362
Is there something you can do
where nobody's in charge, hmm?

102
00:03:48,362 --> 00:03:50,686
- Well, she did leave
us this list of tasks,

103
00:03:50,686 --> 00:03:52,327
perhaps we could divide those up.

104
00:03:52,327 --> 00:03:53,610
- Fine, you're not in charge.

105
00:03:53,610 --> 00:03:54,944
He's not in charge.

106
00:03:54,944 --> 00:03:56,996
- Oh, great, many of these tasks seem

107
00:03:56,996 --> 00:03:58,553
to pertain to you, Bobo.

108
00:03:58,553 --> 00:03:59,944
- Well, I'm very delicate.

109
00:03:59,944 --> 00:04:02,070
- Each morning begins
with a tick bath for Bobo,

110
00:04:02,070 --> 00:04:03,813
then while he's still groggy,

111
00:04:03,813 --> 00:04:06,298
push worm medicine down his throat.

112
00:04:06,298 --> 00:04:07,650
- I have worms (laughing).

113
00:04:07,650 --> 00:04:10,587
- Then mash 65 bananas by
hand, cover with honey,

114
00:04:10,587 --> 00:04:12,882
and sprinkle with termites.

115
00:04:12,882 --> 00:04:14,349
- I won't eat them any other way.

116
00:04:14,349 --> 00:04:17,985
- Then apply a generous
portion of ointment to his--

117
00:04:17,985 --> 00:04:19,154
Oh, no!

118
00:04:19,154 --> 00:04:20,384
- Oh you have to!

119
00:04:20,384 --> 00:04:21,361
- No!

120
00:04:21,361 --> 00:04:23,243
Mike, I can tolerate this ape no more.

121
00:04:23,243 --> 00:04:25,420
I appeal to you as a
somewhat higher being,

122
00:04:25,420 --> 00:04:28,628
promptly come down here, and,
well, just come down here.

123
00:04:28,628 --> 00:04:29,461
(pop)
There you are.

124
00:04:29,461 --> 00:04:30,444
- Ha.

125
00:04:30,444 --> 00:04:33,432
- Now see, he wants me to
apply ointment to his--see.

126
00:04:33,432 --> 00:04:34,696
- Oh come on, it's not so bad.

127
00:04:34,696 --> 00:04:36,520
There are worse places to apply ointment

128
00:04:36,520 --> 00:04:37,353
- Ohohohoho.

129
00:04:37,353 --> 00:04:38,186
- Okay, I'll tell you what I see.

130
00:04:38,186 --> 00:04:40,207
I see here that there are
a lot of underlying issues

131
00:04:40,207 --> 00:04:42,557
and I don't think we can move
on until we get past those.

132
00:04:42,557 --> 00:04:43,390
- Uh-huh.

133
00:04:43,390 --> 00:04:44,703
- Ringo, why don't you start.

134
00:04:44,703 --> 00:04:48,329
- Okay, well, it's like
ever since I met these two,

135
00:04:48,329 --> 00:04:51,115
the whole world revolves
around Bobo's hygiene.

136
00:04:51,115 --> 00:04:54,840
It's endless supply of tick
baths and flea powderings

137
00:04:54,840 --> 00:04:56,641
and swollen things, I just--

138
00:04:56,641 --> 00:04:58,933
- You know, Mike,
sometimes I get the feeling

139
00:04:58,933 --> 00:05:01,082
he doesn't even care about my hygiene.

140
00:05:01,082 --> 00:05:04,583
- Well, frankly his daily
cleaning rituals disgust me.

141
00:05:04,583 --> 00:05:06,750
- Well, at least with me they get done.

142
00:05:06,750 --> 00:05:07,882
- What are you implying?

143
00:05:07,882 --> 00:05:10,454
- I'm implying B.O.!

144
00:05:10,454 --> 00:05:11,287
- B.O?

145
00:05:11,287 --> 00:05:12,120
- Uh-huh uh-huh.

146
00:05:12,120 --> 00:05:13,777
- Well, that's absurd, I
don't even have a body!

147
00:05:13,777 --> 00:05:16,483
- Now, Brain Guy, I think
we need to get past that.

148
00:05:16,483 --> 00:05:19,455
Tell you what, as a gesture,
why don't you smell yourself.

149
00:05:19,455 --> 00:05:20,650
- No!

150
00:05:20,650 --> 00:05:23,929
- Please, in the interest
of peace, smell yourself.

151
00:05:23,929 --> 00:05:25,972
- Oh, very well.

152
00:05:25,972 --> 00:05:26,905
(sniff)

153
00:05:26,905 --> 00:05:28,272
Oh my god, I do stink.

154
00:05:28,272 --> 00:05:31,566
Oh, so sorry, this is embarrassing.

155
00:05:31,566 --> 00:05:33,316
- See, this is a real breakthrough,

156
00:05:33,316 --> 00:05:35,196
I think it's a beautiful moment.

157
00:05:35,196 --> 00:05:37,060
I'll tell you what, why
don't you grab your brain

158
00:05:37,060 --> 00:05:39,824
and head up to the satellite
and watch that movie of yours

159
00:05:39,824 --> 00:05:41,360
and think about this moment.

160
00:05:41,360 --> 00:05:42,462
- Thank, thank you, Mike.

161
00:05:42,462 --> 00:05:44,402
It's called "Jack Frost," by the way,

162
00:05:44,402 --> 00:05:46,309
that's a Russian-Finnish co-production.

163
00:05:46,309 --> 00:05:47,142
- Right.

164
00:05:47,142 --> 00:05:48,652
- Think I will enjoy it immensely.

165
00:05:48,652 --> 00:05:50,485
(laughs) Thank you, thank you for this.

166
00:05:50,485 --> 00:05:51,384
- This is great.

167
00:05:51,384 --> 00:05:52,217
(pop)

168
00:05:52,217 --> 00:05:53,050
- Woohoohoohoo!

169
00:05:53,050 --> 00:05:53,883
(high-five)

170
00:05:53,883 --> 00:05:56,938
Damn, stinky Brain Guy (laughs).

171
00:05:56,938 --> 00:05:58,608
- [Tom] Oh, you do smell, really.

172
00:05:58,608 --> 00:05:59,740
(alarm)
Movie sign!

173
00:05:59,740 --> 00:06:00,573
- Movie sign!

174
00:06:00,573 --> 00:06:01,406
- Movie sign.

175
00:06:01,406 --> 00:06:02,789
Ah!
- Wait a minute, what am I-

176
00:06:02,789 --> 00:06:03,905
Nelson, get up here!

177
00:06:03,905 --> 00:06:05,640
(metal door opens)

178
00:06:05,640 --> 00:06:07,387
(metal squeaks and pops)

179
00:06:07,387 --> 00:06:08,704
(door slams open)

180
00:06:08,704 --> 00:06:09,825
(computer beeps)

181
00:06:09,825 --> 00:06:11,006
(metal door slides)

182
00:06:11,006 --> 00:06:12,040
(beep, beep)

183
00:06:12,040 --> 00:06:13,619
(metal door opens loudly)

184
00:06:13,619 --> 00:06:14,452
(metal door opens)

185
00:06:14,452 --> 00:06:15,472
- [Tom] Oh, good one, Mike.

186
00:06:15,472 --> 00:06:18,259
- (laughs) Yeah, I almost
got the Brain Guy in here.

187
00:06:18,259 --> 00:06:19,250
(soft music)

188
00:06:19,250 --> 00:06:21,500
- [Tom] Could eat no frost.

189
00:06:23,321 --> 00:06:25,349
- [Crow] Oh, (laughs).

190
00:06:25,349 --> 00:06:26,865
- [Mike] These names are all Russian

191
00:06:26,865 --> 00:06:31,048
for Allen Smithy. (laughs)

192
00:06:31,048 --> 00:06:33,219
(snores)

193
00:06:33,219 --> 00:06:34,557
- [Tom] Hey, Tom Petty.

194
00:06:34,557 --> 00:06:37,623
♫ It's alright if you love me ♫

195
00:06:37,623 --> 00:06:39,856
(mosquito)

196
00:06:39,856 --> 00:06:42,364
Hey listen, it's Spock
in really fast motion.

197
00:06:42,364 --> 00:06:43,265
(snores)

198
00:06:43,265 --> 00:06:44,098
(sneezes)

199
00:06:44,098 --> 00:06:45,505
- [Tom] Ah, Rosanne,

200
00:06:45,505 --> 00:06:47,960
- [Mike] My (mumbles) daughter has a cold.

201
00:06:47,960 --> 00:06:50,561
- [Woman On Screen] Hey, come
on, old man, steal yourself.

202
00:06:50,561 --> 00:06:52,056
- (man groans)

203
00:06:52,056 --> 00:06:55,069
- [Crow] C'mon, I wanna reproduce again.

204
00:06:55,069 --> 00:06:56,372
- [Woman On Screen] The
mosquitoes are stinging

205
00:06:56,372 --> 00:06:57,639
my darling little Marfushka, okay?

206
00:06:57,639 --> 00:06:58,910
And I can't sleep.

207
00:06:58,910 --> 00:07:01,089
- Oh, no listen (clears throat), alright,

208
00:07:01,089 --> 00:07:02,105
I didn't say a word.

209
00:07:02,105 --> 00:07:04,371
- [Tom] Great, I bet Pippy
Longstocking's in this.

210
00:07:04,371 --> 00:07:07,280
Tend your koala bear and
eat these eucalyptus leaves.

211
00:07:07,280 --> 00:07:10,168
(Marfushka groans)

212
00:07:10,168 --> 00:07:12,291
- [Tom] Oh, kielbasa belch.

213
00:07:12,291 --> 00:07:13,558
(Woman on Screen sings)

214
00:07:13,558 --> 00:07:17,468
- [Tom] Arsenic sucker, that should do it.

215
00:07:17,468 --> 00:07:21,051
- [Mike] Is this a bio
pic of Holly Hobbie?

216
00:07:22,260 --> 00:07:24,092
- [Tom] The story of a
hundred year old couple

217
00:07:24,092 --> 00:07:26,300
who give birth to a giant infant.

218
00:07:26,300 --> 00:07:27,615
(Woman on screen hums)

219
00:07:27,615 --> 00:07:30,309
(bed squeaks)

220
00:07:30,309 --> 00:07:34,474
- [Crow] Don't wave Grandma's
funk over here, please.

221
00:07:34,474 --> 00:07:37,057
- [Tom] I'm a domestic goddess.

222
00:07:38,113 --> 00:07:39,823
- What are you doing there, Nastenka?

223
00:07:39,823 --> 00:07:42,714
- Just knitting Marfushka's new stocking.

224
00:07:42,714 --> 00:07:43,547
- Knitting it.

225
00:07:43,547 --> 00:07:45,071
- [Tom] Why is the coat rack on fire?

226
00:07:45,071 --> 00:07:46,476
- You told me to knit some stockings--

227
00:07:46,476 --> 00:07:47,317
- Be quiet.

228
00:07:47,317 --> 00:07:48,476
- [Crow] All you novitiates are trouble.

229
00:07:48,476 --> 00:07:51,282
- I told you to knit, but I never told you

230
00:07:51,282 --> 00:07:53,425
to click your needles like that, did I?

231
00:07:53,425 --> 00:07:55,952
Before you know, you'll
wake my little darling.

232
00:07:55,952 --> 00:07:58,717
- Can she really hear
that through those walls?

233
00:07:58,717 --> 00:07:59,991
- She certainly can!
- [Crow] Ah!

234
00:07:59,991 --> 00:08:01,883
- You work by day like a young man

235
00:08:01,883 --> 00:08:02,984
so you can sleep by night.

236
00:08:02,984 --> 00:08:03,817
- [Crow] Ah.

237
00:08:03,817 --> 00:08:05,452
- My little Marfushka cannot be a man.

238
00:08:05,452 --> 00:08:08,296
She must not be, she has
to rest by day so at night

239
00:08:08,296 --> 00:08:10,167
the slightest noise wakes her.

240
00:08:10,167 --> 00:08:11,923
(blows)

241
00:08:11,923 --> 00:08:13,562
- [Tom] Um, panic cooking?

242
00:08:13,562 --> 00:08:15,255
- [Crow] Let's go eat some fish.

243
00:08:15,255 --> 00:08:17,166
(footsteps)

244
00:08:17,166 --> 00:08:18,107
(door opens)

245
00:08:18,107 --> 00:08:20,292
- Here's a place where
you can knit Nastenka,

246
00:08:20,292 --> 00:08:23,335
and you won't wake my
darling little Marfushka.

247
00:08:23,335 --> 00:08:25,312
The moon is out. There's plenty of light.

248
00:08:25,312 --> 00:08:27,295
- [Mike] The mobile's on fire, it's great.

249
00:08:27,295 --> 00:08:30,426
- It's peaceful and it's nice and cooler.

250
00:08:30,426 --> 00:08:31,259
(dog barks)

251
00:08:31,259 --> 00:08:32,092
- [Tom] Beat it, Grandma.

252
00:08:32,092 --> 00:08:33,008
- Be quiet.

253
00:08:33,008 --> 00:08:34,274
(dog growls lowly)
- [Mike] Back into Harpo's

254
00:08:34,274 --> 00:08:35,179
chest.

255
00:08:35,179 --> 00:08:36,578
- You give me so much work.

256
00:08:36,578 --> 00:08:39,865
- [Crow] This is the factory
where they make Beanie Babies.

257
00:08:39,865 --> 00:08:41,148
- [Tom] Jack Klugman.

258
00:08:41,148 --> 00:08:43,138
- You must be finished by
the time the rooster crows,

259
00:08:43,138 --> 00:08:43,971
you hear me?

260
00:08:43,971 --> 00:08:45,172
- [Crow] Okay Mom, thanks.

261
00:08:45,172 --> 00:08:46,928
- Otherwise my precious little girl,

262
00:08:46,928 --> 00:08:49,147
I will tear your braid off.

263
00:08:49,147 --> 00:08:51,739
- [Crow] ♫ M is for the
many times you beat me ♫

264
00:08:51,739 --> 00:08:52,829
(door closes)

265
00:08:52,829 --> 00:08:54,529
♫ O is for the other times you beat me ♫

266
00:08:54,529 --> 00:08:55,779
- Jappa, Jappa.

267
00:08:57,510 --> 00:08:59,915
(soft music)

268
00:08:59,915 --> 00:09:00,748
Shh.

269
00:09:00,748 --> 00:09:02,499
(man groans)

270
00:09:02,499 --> 00:09:04,959
- [Crow] Oh, their other puppy, he's cute.

271
00:09:04,959 --> 00:09:07,141
- [Crow] I gotta sneak down
to the convenience store

272
00:09:07,141 --> 00:09:09,058
and go to the bathroom.

273
00:09:10,915 --> 00:09:13,789
- [Mike] I wish she'd take
that mouse out of her mouth.

274
00:09:13,789 --> 00:09:14,630
(slurps)

275
00:09:14,630 --> 00:09:18,425
- [Tom] ♫ Don't come around here no more ♫

276
00:09:18,425 --> 00:09:21,800
- [Crow] You keep knitting
and knitting and knitting.

277
00:09:21,800 --> 00:09:23,533
(snores)

278
00:09:23,533 --> 00:09:27,700
- [Crow] Ah, Penny Marshall
was an adorable child.

279
00:09:28,740 --> 00:09:29,791
- [Tom] You want a stinkin' sock?

280
00:09:29,791 --> 00:09:33,109
I'll knit you a stinkin' sock,
here's your stinkin' sock.

281
00:09:33,109 --> 00:09:36,893
- [Crow] Oh, those are fly
specks they've been aiming.

282
00:09:36,893 --> 00:09:41,079
- [Mike] She's so hideous when she sleeps.

283
00:09:41,079 --> 00:09:42,246
- [Tom] Surge!

284
00:09:45,628 --> 00:09:48,128
- [Crow] Mm, liver on a stick.

285
00:09:49,824 --> 00:09:53,324
- [Tom] Danny Bonaduce is Sleeping Beauty.

286
00:09:54,918 --> 00:09:59,832
- [Crow] With God as my witness,
I'll never go hungry again.

287
00:09:59,832 --> 00:10:02,988
So, the first plot point
involves knitting socks.

288
00:10:02,988 --> 00:10:04,371
I think we're in for quite a ride, guys.

289
00:10:04,371 --> 00:10:05,755
- [Mike] You bet.

290
00:10:05,755 --> 00:10:06,930
(wings flutter)

291
00:10:06,930 --> 00:10:09,347
- [Voiceover] Boy, I say boy.

292
00:10:10,383 --> 00:10:11,727
- Down, Tanushka.

293
00:10:11,727 --> 00:10:13,720
- [Crow] It's Rex, ma'am

294
00:10:13,720 --> 00:10:14,819
(squawk)

295
00:10:14,819 --> 00:10:17,595
- Give me a little time,
please pretty rooster.

296
00:10:17,595 --> 00:10:19,962
Please, I've only got one row to knit.

297
00:10:19,962 --> 00:10:24,129
(indiscernible rooster chatter)

298
00:10:25,629 --> 00:10:29,791
- [Crow] You can talk to
my supervisor if you like.

299
00:10:29,791 --> 00:10:32,337
- [Tom] Mm, Claritin-D.

300
00:10:32,337 --> 00:10:35,587
- [Mike] Wow, the sun's really bookin'.

301
00:10:37,445 --> 00:10:38,768
- [Tom] Chickens, lock up your daughters,

302
00:10:38,768 --> 00:10:42,324
I'm on the prowl (laughs).

303
00:10:42,324 --> 00:10:44,786
Hey, hey, honey, where ya
going, you wanna come in?

304
00:10:44,786 --> 00:10:47,786
(running footsteps)

305
00:10:48,831 --> 00:10:51,240
- [Crow] Oh, she's mooning us.

306
00:10:51,240 --> 00:10:53,394
- Have mercy, rosy fingered dawn.

307
00:10:53,394 --> 00:10:56,162
Have mercy on me, oh rising golden sun.

308
00:10:56,162 --> 00:10:57,348
- [Tom] And you are?

309
00:10:57,348 --> 00:10:59,697
- Wait 'til I'm done
knitting these stockings.

310
00:10:59,697 --> 00:11:02,378
Otherwise I'll be punished severely.

311
00:11:02,378 --> 00:11:05,710
Stepmother said she
will tear off my braid.

312
00:11:05,710 --> 00:11:07,982
- [Crow] (whistle) This
is the sun, your call

313
00:11:07,982 --> 00:11:09,213
is very important to us,

314
00:11:09,213 --> 00:11:12,785
but due to an unusually
high call volume...

315
00:11:12,785 --> 00:11:14,237
- [Tom] Oh, the world's
turning into chaos,

316
00:11:14,237 --> 00:11:15,628
earthquakes, flood, but that's fine,

317
00:11:15,628 --> 00:11:17,110
you knit your sock.

318
00:11:17,110 --> 00:11:20,027
(soft piano music)

319
00:11:22,804 --> 00:11:24,821
- [Nastenka] Thank you rosy fingered dawn.

320
00:11:24,821 --> 00:11:26,649
- [Crow] Some day I'll return the favor.

321
00:11:26,649 --> 00:11:27,482
(rooster squawks)

322
00:11:27,482 --> 00:11:28,972
- [Crow] Now I've gotta
keep stirring the sauce,

323
00:11:28,972 --> 00:11:31,240
deliver these guns to Jimmy, and uh--

324
00:11:31,240 --> 00:11:32,306
- [Tom] I heard that.

325
00:11:32,306 --> 00:11:34,690
- [Nastenka] My darling
bird with the golden cone

326
00:11:34,690 --> 00:11:35,771
(rooster squawks)

327
00:11:35,771 --> 00:11:37,557
I'm so happy, my pretty one.

328
00:11:37,557 --> 00:11:39,095
Thank you, it's done.

329
00:11:39,095 --> 00:11:40,698
- [Tom] Yeah, sure, do
you know any foxy hens?

330
00:11:40,698 --> 00:11:41,531
Hey.

331
00:11:41,531 --> 00:11:43,454
- You see, I'm finished.

332
00:11:43,454 --> 00:11:46,578
- You lazy girl, have you finished yet?

333
00:11:46,578 --> 00:11:47,625
- Look.

334
00:11:47,625 --> 00:11:50,341
- So you did it on time,
why you wicked little viper,

335
00:11:50,341 --> 00:11:52,256
you, you wicked little witch.

336
00:11:52,256 --> 00:11:54,498
I'll give you much harder work next time.

337
00:11:54,498 --> 00:11:57,112
In the mean time, go feed the
chickens, water the cattles,

338
00:11:57,112 --> 00:11:59,343
split the wood, and sweep the yard.

339
00:11:59,343 --> 00:12:00,176
- Oh.

340
00:12:00,176 --> 00:12:01,009
- [Crow] You know, Mike,

341
00:12:01,009 --> 00:12:05,168
I think I just don't like
evil Russo Finnish grandmas.

342
00:12:05,168 --> 00:12:07,111
♫ Take this job and shove it ♫

343
00:12:07,111 --> 00:12:08,794
- Yeah, bushka,
(dog whines)

344
00:12:08,794 --> 00:12:09,952
(rooster crows)

345
00:12:09,952 --> 00:12:12,139
- [Crow] How 'bout a little
sugar for the rooster?

346
00:12:12,139 --> 00:12:12,972
(rooster crows)

347
00:12:12,972 --> 00:12:16,001
- [Crow] This is a test of the
emergency broadcast chicken.

348
00:12:16,001 --> 00:12:17,297
(rooster crows)

349
00:12:17,297 --> 00:12:18,722
- [Tom] Man, Peter must be walking

350
00:12:18,722 --> 00:12:21,387
around denying everybody this morning.

351
00:12:21,387 --> 00:12:24,167
(rooster Crow)

352
00:12:24,167 --> 00:12:28,798
- [Voiceover] On the very same
morning of the very same day.

353
00:12:28,798 --> 00:12:32,205
- [Tom] (clears throat and
Crows like a rooster) (laughs).

354
00:12:32,205 --> 00:12:33,038
- [Mike] Mornin'

355
00:12:33,038 --> 00:12:34,288
- [Tom] Mornin'

356
00:12:36,342 --> 00:12:38,896
- [Crow] Hey, watch it.

357
00:12:38,896 --> 00:12:40,338
(chicken clucks)

358
00:12:40,338 --> 00:12:42,101
- [Tom] Well, the chores
are done for the day,

359
00:12:42,101 --> 00:12:44,942
I think I'll go nap off
a bottle of Finlandia.

360
00:12:44,942 --> 00:12:47,155
- [Mike] He's got June Allison hair.

361
00:12:47,155 --> 00:12:48,669
- [Crow] (laughs)

362
00:12:48,669 --> 00:12:49,814
- Ivan, my son.

363
00:12:49,814 --> 00:12:51,500
- Yes, Mama, what is it now?

364
00:12:51,500 --> 00:12:53,483
- [Crow] Bring these bags to be recycled.

365
00:12:53,483 --> 00:12:55,215
- You must take care.

366
00:12:55,215 --> 00:12:56,382
- Don't worry.

367
00:12:57,596 --> 00:13:00,067
- You mustn't forget your mother, Ivan.

368
00:13:00,067 --> 00:13:01,090
- [Ivan] Don't worry.

369
00:13:01,090 --> 00:13:02,416
- [Crow] Or me, Jerry Quarry.

370
00:13:02,416 --> 00:13:03,866
- You mustn't harm the weak.

371
00:13:03,866 --> 00:13:05,588
- [Ivan] Don't worry!

372
00:13:05,588 --> 00:13:07,757
- Honor those who are old.

373
00:13:07,757 --> 00:13:08,973
- [Ivan] Don't worry.

374
00:13:08,973 --> 00:13:11,571
- [Crow] Just going to get a paper.

375
00:13:11,571 --> 00:13:15,452
And I even made him
Lunchables (pretend crying).

376
00:13:15,452 --> 00:13:17,533
- [Group Of Men] We will
rob him, we won't rob him,

377
00:13:17,533 --> 00:13:18,366
- [Tom] Damn hobbits.

378
00:13:18,366 --> 00:13:21,658
- [Men] we will eat
them, we won't eat them--

379
00:13:21,658 --> 00:13:23,399
- [Crow] The Ozark
Mountain Daredevils plan

380
00:13:23,399 --> 00:13:24,695
their next album.

381
00:13:24,695 --> 00:13:26,353
- [Men] will be eaten (growl).

382
00:13:26,353 --> 00:13:27,837
- [Crow] Oh sorry, that was me.

383
00:13:27,837 --> 00:13:30,159
- [Men] We will rob him, we won't rob him,

384
00:13:30,159 --> 00:13:33,244
we will eat them, we won't eat them--

385
00:13:33,244 --> 00:13:34,832
- [Crow] Hey, wake up and go to sleep.

386
00:13:34,832 --> 00:13:37,874
- [Tom] Oh oh oh oh oh, look.

387
00:13:37,874 --> 00:13:38,924
- [Men] We will rob them.

388
00:13:38,924 --> 00:13:41,377
- [Crow] Mm, that's their outhouse.

389
00:13:41,377 --> 00:13:42,912
- [Tom] Why?

390
00:13:42,912 --> 00:13:44,420
Finland is bad this year.

391
00:13:44,420 --> 00:13:47,125
(groans)

392
00:13:47,125 --> 00:13:49,446
- [Crow] Oh wait, today it's clock clock.

393
00:13:49,446 --> 00:13:51,696
(whistles)

394
00:13:52,823 --> 00:13:56,370
- [Crow] Um, I lost a Titleist
three down here, anyone?

395
00:13:56,370 --> 00:13:59,277
- [Mike] This is the early
version of Snow White,

396
00:13:59,277 --> 00:14:03,106
called "Snow White and the
One Normal-Size Person."

397
00:14:03,106 --> 00:14:05,525
- [Tom] Oh what a beautiful
(nonsensical words),

398
00:14:05,525 --> 00:14:07,876
oh what a beautiful (nonsensical words)

399
00:14:07,876 --> 00:14:10,744
(whistles)

400
00:14:10,744 --> 00:14:12,365
- [Mike] A wandering youth minister.

401
00:14:12,365 --> 00:14:14,445
(whistles)

402
00:14:14,445 --> 00:14:15,955
- Halt!

403
00:14:15,955 --> 00:14:16,788
- Halt!

404
00:14:16,788 --> 00:14:18,519
- [Crow] Get a haircut, hippie.

405
00:14:18,519 --> 00:14:20,827
(horses run)

406
00:14:20,827 --> 00:14:21,943
- You're captured!

407
00:14:21,943 --> 00:14:22,862
- [Crow] The human schnauzer.

408
00:14:22,862 --> 00:14:25,340
- And now, young man,
we're going to rob you.

409
00:14:25,340 --> 00:14:26,342
- You mean that?

410
00:14:26,342 --> 00:14:27,382
- Yes, we do.

411
00:14:27,382 --> 00:14:28,313
- [Tom] Ah, ha.

412
00:14:28,313 --> 00:14:30,555
- Alright, rob me.

413
00:14:30,555 --> 00:14:32,912
- [Crow] I'll strip if you want me to.

414
00:14:32,912 --> 00:14:35,135
(Group of men yell)

415
00:14:35,135 --> 00:14:36,621
You know, I think I'd rather be hog piled

416
00:14:36,621 --> 00:14:37,855
by actual hogs.

417
00:14:37,855 --> 00:14:39,668
- [Tom] (laughs)

418
00:14:39,668 --> 00:14:42,501
(high-tech music)

419
00:14:45,848 --> 00:14:47,548
(group of men yell)

420
00:14:47,548 --> 00:14:51,715
- [Crow] Wow, that's the
biggest clove I've ever seen.

421
00:14:51,715 --> 00:14:54,064
- [Tom] Uh-oh, he's
ignoring his mom's advice,

422
00:14:54,064 --> 00:14:55,830
don't throw cudgels in the air.

423
00:14:55,830 --> 00:14:59,434
(men chatter in background)

424
00:14:59,434 --> 00:15:03,601
- [Crow] Uh, did somebody
drop some femurs over here?

425
00:15:04,792 --> 00:15:08,959
- [Tom] I think he's missed
the point of juggling.

426
00:15:10,164 --> 00:15:12,626
- [Mike] And they're frantically
hoping he has a louse comb.

427
00:15:12,626 --> 00:15:14,870
(men argue)

428
00:15:14,870 --> 00:15:16,370
He's got Playboys.

429
00:15:17,942 --> 00:15:20,325
- [Tom] I'm gonna keep doing
this 'til someone notices me.

430
00:15:20,325 --> 00:15:22,039
- [Crow] Then celebrate the new year

431
00:15:22,039 --> 00:15:24,464
by hurling giant beef
steaks high into the air.

432
00:15:24,464 --> 00:15:26,955
(rising music)

433
00:15:26,955 --> 00:15:31,304
- [Tom] Wow, listen to
the bass on those cudgels.

434
00:15:31,304 --> 00:15:33,046
- [Crow] You didn't tell
us you were mystical.

435
00:15:33,046 --> 00:15:35,137
- Why don't those clubs come down again?

436
00:15:35,137 --> 00:15:38,021
- (laughs) Just wait my
eager little bandits.

437
00:15:38,021 --> 00:15:39,896
They'll come home next winter.

438
00:15:39,896 --> 00:15:40,992
- Next winter?

439
00:15:40,992 --> 00:15:42,049
- That's right

440
00:15:42,049 --> 00:15:42,882
[Man] Oh.

441
00:15:42,882 --> 00:15:44,188
- [Tom] Now quit bouncing
and behaving, boy.

442
00:15:44,188 --> 00:15:46,767
(whistles)

443
00:15:46,767 --> 00:15:48,530
- Next winter, he says.

444
00:15:48,530 --> 00:15:50,382
- Did you see that,
men, that takes muscle.

445
00:15:50,382 --> 00:15:51,629
He's strong alright.

446
00:15:51,629 --> 00:15:53,660
(men all chatter at once)

447
00:15:53,660 --> 00:15:55,108
- [Crow] (barking like a dog)

448
00:15:55,108 --> 00:15:56,149
- That's odd.

449
00:15:56,149 --> 00:15:58,976
- [Crow] The guy you told, dwarfs.

450
00:15:58,976 --> 00:16:02,092
- [Voiceover] How long
did our young hero, Ivan,

451
00:16:02,092 --> 00:16:05,955
wander over hill and dell,
frankly, we have no idea.

452
00:16:05,955 --> 00:16:06,788
- [Tom] Who's talking?

453
00:16:06,788 --> 00:16:07,621
- [Crow] (laughs)

454
00:16:07,621 --> 00:16:09,653
- [Voiceover] The fact remains
that Ivan eventually reached

455
00:16:09,653 --> 00:16:11,903
far away and unknown lands.

456
00:16:13,580 --> 00:16:15,280
- [Mike] And the cudgels
came down way earlier

457
00:16:15,280 --> 00:16:17,521
the next winter and
named several children.

458
00:16:17,521 --> 00:16:19,354
(upbeat dreamy music)

459
00:16:19,354 --> 00:16:20,949
- Ivan Rushka.

460
00:16:20,949 --> 00:16:23,635
- [Crow] I have a new church hat.

461
00:16:23,635 --> 00:16:27,802
- [Tom] Yeah, I've eaten
those and had this happen.

462
00:16:28,682 --> 00:16:30,828
- [Voiceover] Ivan Rushka,

463
00:16:30,828 --> 00:16:33,912
- [Tom] So what does a mushroom
eat for hallucinations?

464
00:16:33,912 --> 00:16:37,186
- [Crow] I think they lick toads.

465
00:16:37,186 --> 00:16:38,518
- [Voiceover] Ivan Rushka.

466
00:16:38,518 --> 00:16:40,063
- [Tom] My hair was talking to me.

467
00:16:40,063 --> 00:16:41,894
(dreamy music)

468
00:16:41,894 --> 00:16:44,646
- [Mike] Nah, I always pick
that little guy off my pizza.

469
00:16:44,646 --> 00:16:48,567
- [Crow] Ivan Rushka,
try me on a plaza burger.

470
00:16:48,567 --> 00:16:50,924
- [Tom] Are you freaking out yet?

471
00:16:50,924 --> 00:16:54,115
- [Ivan] Alright, who's playing
hide and seek with me now?

472
00:16:54,115 --> 00:16:56,615
(Tom mumbles)

473
00:16:58,747 --> 00:16:59,580
- You?

474
00:16:59,580 --> 00:17:00,413
- [Tom] Cute outfit.

475
00:17:00,413 --> 00:17:01,454
- [Mushroom] Yes.

476
00:17:01,454 --> 00:17:03,502
- Are you a sorcerer, Granddaddy?

477
00:17:03,502 --> 00:17:05,150
- I dabble in sorcery a little,

478
00:17:05,150 --> 00:17:08,044
but the truth is, that I get bored.

479
00:17:08,044 --> 00:17:09,104
- You get bored?

480
00:17:09,104 --> 00:17:10,246
- I get bored.

481
00:17:10,246 --> 00:17:11,146
- [Crow] You get bored?

482
00:17:11,146 --> 00:17:12,478
- Come on, play with me, lets play hide

483
00:17:12,478 --> 00:17:13,311
and seek together.

484
00:17:13,311 --> 00:17:15,011
- (laughs) With you?

485
00:17:15,011 --> 00:17:15,945
Play hide and seek?

486
00:17:15,945 --> 00:17:17,628
- [Granddad] Yes.
- You're joking.

487
00:17:17,628 --> 00:17:18,987
I'd catch you in no time.

488
00:17:18,987 --> 00:17:19,820
- Think so?

489
00:17:19,820 --> 00:17:20,653
- Yes, I think so.

490
00:17:20,653 --> 00:17:23,173
- If you catch me, I'll
give you a well-bent bow

491
00:17:23,173 --> 00:17:24,788
and some nice straight arrows.

492
00:17:24,788 --> 00:17:25,621
Is that a bargain?

493
00:17:25,621 --> 00:17:26,971
- It's a bargain, Father Mushroom.

494
00:17:26,971 --> 00:17:28,314
- [Crow] I thought Jerry Garcia

495
00:17:28,314 --> 00:17:30,442
was Father Mushroom (laughs).

496
00:17:30,442 --> 00:17:33,359
- [Tom] Finally I have a boyfriend.

497
00:17:35,197 --> 00:17:37,122
I'm Hans, oh forget it.

498
00:17:37,122 --> 00:17:38,752
- [Crow] I'm gonna go
hunt for your cousin,

499
00:17:38,752 --> 00:17:40,002
Cornsmut, instead.

500
00:17:40,002 --> 00:17:42,451
(upbeat dreamy music)

501
00:17:42,451 --> 00:17:45,235
- [Tom] You twisted little
woodear, I'm gonna--

502
00:17:45,235 --> 00:17:47,152
(hums)

503
00:17:48,485 --> 00:17:50,485
- [Mike] Frodo gets drunk and
screws with his neighbors.

504
00:17:50,485 --> 00:17:53,485
(dreamy harp music)

505
00:17:55,645 --> 00:17:58,713
