- [Tom] Oh, I'm very intolerant.

751
00:27:15,690 --> 00:27:18,107
(slow music)

752
00:27:19,114 --> 00:27:20,543
Oh, salmon breath.

753
00:27:20,543 --> 00:27:23,376
- [Tom] Let me get you some grubs.

754
00:27:24,635 --> 00:27:25,783
- [Crow] You looks at your lips

755
00:27:25,783 --> 00:27:28,347
and tell me if you're breathing?

756
00:27:28,347 --> 00:27:30,950
- [Ivan] She is alive.

757
00:27:30,950 --> 00:27:35,117
- [Tom] Oh no, I lost my hat!
(growling)

758
00:27:38,075 --> 00:27:41,024
- [Crow] Dammit puck, this
time you've gone too far.

759
00:27:41,024 --> 00:27:42,983
- [Ivan] What did you do to me?

760
00:27:42,983 --> 00:27:45,923
What have you done, you witch?

761
00:27:45,923 --> 00:27:47,771
- [Tom] Mommy (fake crying).

762
00:27:47,771 --> 00:27:50,938
I've gotta go find a pic-a-nic basket.

763
00:27:52,368 --> 00:27:53,601
- [Nastenka] Ivan Rushka!

764
00:27:53,601 --> 00:27:55,348
- [Crow] We have to register at club wed!

765
00:27:55,348 --> 00:27:56,181
- [Nastenka] Ivan Rushka,

766
00:27:56,181 --> 00:27:57,778
I swear I didn't do anything to you!

767
00:27:57,778 --> 00:28:01,797
- [Ivan] I curse you, I curse you forever!

768
00:28:01,797 --> 00:28:02,630
You witch!

769
00:28:04,714 --> 00:28:05,943
(growling)

770
00:28:05,943 --> 00:28:08,752
- [Tom] Hey, you can always
get a job as a sports mascot.

771
00:28:08,752 --> 00:28:11,150
Tonight on a very special "Grizzly Adams".

772
00:28:11,150 --> 00:28:12,023
(Ivan growling)

773
00:28:12,023 --> 00:28:13,606
- [Crow] Panakuken.

774
00:28:14,607 --> 00:28:18,774
- [Mike] Every time I meet a
man he's either gay or a bear.

775
00:28:20,043 --> 00:28:23,293
- [Tom] A tribute to eurasian nailfoil.

776
00:28:25,043 --> 00:28:27,250
- [Crow] With retsin.

777
00:28:27,250 --> 00:28:29,500
Again, with retsin.

778
00:28:29,500 --> 00:28:30,333
Retsin.

779
00:28:34,307 --> 00:28:37,354
- [Crow] The KGB has
her under surveillance!

780
00:28:37,354 --> 00:28:41,521
(dreamy music)
- [Tom] (humming with music)

781
00:28:43,940 --> 00:28:45,190
- [Crow] Gross.

782
00:28:48,329 --> 00:28:52,805
I should've married
him, I'm getting so old.

783
00:28:52,805 --> 00:28:55,055
(Tom hums)

784
00:28:56,404 --> 00:28:57,670
Well, she shouldn't cry,

785
00:28:57,670 --> 00:28:59,905
there's always Jerry Lee
Lewis, or Jerry Seinfeld,

786
00:28:59,905 --> 00:29:03,396
or Ben Kingsley (laughs).

787
00:29:03,396 --> 00:29:05,843
- [Mike] Hello, hello.

788
00:29:05,843 --> 00:29:07,431
Russo-Finnish co-production?

789
00:29:07,431 --> 00:29:08,531
(Ivan hums)

790
00:29:08,531 --> 00:29:10,658
- [Crow] Mm, get me some
french-fried potatoes mm.

791
00:29:10,658 --> 00:29:14,719
- [Ivan] I kill you with
an arrow and you ruin me

792
00:29:14,719 --> 00:29:16,072
with a feather.

793
00:29:16,072 --> 00:29:17,689
- [Mike] It's funny
when you think about it.

794
00:29:17,689 --> 00:29:19,401
(Ivan groaning)

795
00:29:19,401 --> 00:29:20,292
- [Tom] You know, back
when they didn't know

796
00:29:20,292 --> 00:29:22,423
about costuming, they actually had to find

797
00:29:22,423 --> 00:29:24,256
a half-man, half-bear.

798
00:29:26,228 --> 00:29:27,504
- [Crow] I've got to learn how to ride

799
00:29:27,504 --> 00:29:29,863
a tricycle in a hurry.

800
00:29:29,863 --> 00:29:31,865
Warning, hang trees in food, hey.

801
00:29:31,865 --> 00:29:35,839
- [Ivan] Like a bear, you
wouldn't have the head of a bear.

802
00:29:35,839 --> 00:29:38,262
- [Tom] Forgot to read the fine ruins.

803
00:29:38,262 --> 00:29:40,167
(ominous music)

804
00:29:40,167 --> 00:29:43,220
- [Mike] Sort of a bloated
mouth-breathing bear, but a bear.

805
00:29:43,220 --> 00:29:44,844
(Ivan groans)

806
00:29:44,844 --> 00:29:48,089
- [Father Mushroom] Ivan,
Ivan with the head of a bear.

807
00:29:48,089 --> 00:29:49,485
- [Crow] Yeah, bite me, Wokhead.

808
00:29:49,485 --> 00:29:52,766
- Forgive me Father
Mushroom, forgive me, please.

809
00:29:52,766 --> 00:29:55,401
- You see, Ivan, things have come to pass

810
00:29:55,401 --> 00:29:58,239
amd the bear bows his head to the ground,

811
00:29:58,239 --> 00:30:01,114
but it's your back that bends.

812
00:30:01,114 --> 00:30:03,660
- Oh, teach me how to be reasonable and

813
00:30:03,660 --> 00:30:07,435
first of all, tell me
exactly what I should do so

814
00:30:07,435 --> 00:30:09,510
that I may be a man again.

815
00:30:09,510 --> 00:30:13,328
- Alright listen, vagabond
with the head of a bear,

816
00:30:13,328 --> 00:30:15,882
just look at yourself and ask--

817
00:30:15,882 --> 00:30:17,115
- [Tom] Do I crap in the woods?

818
00:30:17,115 --> 00:30:18,124
- How did you live?

819
00:30:18,124 --> 00:30:21,843
You see you spent all of your
time boasting to everybody.

820
00:30:21,843 --> 00:30:23,290
You loved yourself.

821
00:30:23,290 --> 00:30:26,977
You loved only yourself,
you offended everyone else.

822
00:30:26,977 --> 00:30:28,820
- [Crow] Heed these words, Mike.

823
00:30:28,820 --> 00:30:30,786
- Your hurt her feelings.

824
00:30:30,786 --> 00:30:32,743
- I hurt her feelings?

825
00:30:32,743 --> 00:30:34,123
- [Father Mushroom] Ah, you've never done

826
00:30:34,123 --> 00:30:37,279
a good deed, Ivan-- now here's my answer.

827
00:30:37,279 --> 00:30:40,941
Here's my advice to you,
although I'm wondering

828
00:30:40,941 --> 00:30:43,086
whether you can understand it.

829
00:30:43,086 --> 00:30:45,308
- [Ivan] Of course I understand it.

830
00:30:45,308 --> 00:30:46,141
- [Mike] I'm a great understander.

831
00:30:46,141 --> 00:30:48,156
- I'll just go and do a good deed.

832
00:30:48,156 --> 00:30:51,591
When I've done a good deed,
I'll get my own head back.

833
00:30:51,591 --> 00:30:55,163
- Ivan, Ivan!

834
00:30:55,163 --> 00:30:59,059
- [Crow] You can make a
lot of money wrestling.

835
00:30:59,059 --> 00:31:00,955
- You haven't understood anything.

836
00:31:00,955 --> 00:31:01,788
(explosion)

837
00:31:01,788 --> 00:31:02,621
- [Tom] Oh, I didn't know

838
00:31:02,621 --> 00:31:05,749
there were that many land
mines left in Narnia.

839
00:31:05,749 --> 00:31:08,582
(high-tech music)

840
00:31:11,745 --> 00:31:12,915
(upbeat flute music)

841
00:31:12,915 --> 00:31:15,289
- [Father Mushroom] Oh but I like it, too.

842
00:31:15,289 --> 00:31:19,460
- [Crow] Hello, Jeremy, what
good deeds can I do for you?

843
00:31:19,460 --> 00:31:20,964
- [Mike] Well, you can stop crapping

844
00:31:20,964 --> 00:31:22,122
on our playground, for one.

845
00:31:22,122 --> 00:31:22,969
(children yelling)

846
00:31:22,969 --> 00:31:26,460
- [Ivan] Stop! Wait!

847
00:31:26,460 --> 00:31:27,714
Don't run away!

848
00:31:27,714 --> 00:31:29,179
- [Tom] He's out running a
really slow quarter horse

849
00:31:29,179 --> 00:31:30,012
at this point.

850
00:31:30,012 --> 00:31:33,995
- [Ivan] Wait, I want to
do a good deed for you!

851
00:31:33,995 --> 00:31:36,931
Wait! Wait!

852
00:31:36,931 --> 00:31:38,740
- [Crow] When animals attack.

853
00:31:38,740 --> 00:31:41,073
Now go into slow motion and
you'll hear Barber's adagio

854
00:31:41,073 --> 00:31:43,408
for strings as he tears them apart.

855
00:31:43,408 --> 00:31:45,278
(children yelling)

856
00:31:45,278 --> 00:31:46,572
- [Ivan] Ohhhh!

857
00:31:46,572 --> 00:31:50,485
- [Tom] Now he falls right on bear plop.

858
00:31:50,485 --> 00:31:53,402
- [Crow] Um, Ricola, Mueslix?

859
00:31:54,992 --> 00:31:58,124
- [Tom] Charlie was
close, I could feel it.

860
00:31:58,124 --> 00:31:59,957
Oh, there's my wallet.

861
00:32:02,067 --> 00:32:05,152
- [Crow] As the Easter egg
hunt goes into its 48th week.

862
00:32:05,152 --> 00:32:07,258
(bear growling)

863
00:32:07,258 --> 00:32:08,925
- [Tom] Friend good.

864
00:32:10,597 --> 00:32:12,850
Ah, the perfect speaker stand finally.

865
00:32:12,850 --> 00:32:16,744
And here that foot stool
I've always wanted.

866
00:32:16,744 --> 00:32:17,930
- [Crow] Ah, you know?

867
00:32:17,930 --> 00:32:19,823
- [Tom] Ah (laughs).

868
00:32:19,823 --> 00:32:20,656
(bear growling)

869
00:32:20,656 --> 00:32:24,259
- [All Three] Awwww (laugh).

870
00:32:24,259 --> 00:32:25,828
- [Mike] I'll take this back to the lab

871
00:32:25,828 --> 00:32:28,664
and see if it's edible or not.

872
00:32:28,664 --> 00:32:30,563
- [Tom] Hurry, the DNR's coming,

873
00:32:30,563 --> 00:32:33,135
load up the truck and get outta here.

874
00:32:33,135 --> 00:32:33,968
(both girls screaming)

875
00:32:33,968 --> 00:32:36,026
- [Crow] Icky, boys, eww!

876
00:32:36,026 --> 00:32:38,943
- [Mike] Delayed reaction syndrome.

877
00:32:40,431 --> 00:32:42,916
- [Both Girls] There's a bear!

878
00:32:42,916 --> 00:32:44,279
- [Tom] Quick, there's a sale on babushkas

879
00:32:44,279 --> 00:32:46,949
at Bloomingdales, please (laughs).

880
00:32:46,949 --> 00:32:48,424
(girls scream)

881
00:32:48,424 --> 00:32:51,259
- [Crow] Chernoble's exploding
again, let's go watch!

882
00:32:51,259 --> 00:32:52,092
(girls scream)

883
00:32:52,092 --> 00:32:54,896
- [Tom] I could watch this
scene play out all day.

884
00:32:54,896 --> 00:32:56,291
(birds chirp)

885
00:32:56,291 --> 00:32:59,124
- [Mike] Well, how not to be seen.

886
00:33:02,276 --> 00:33:05,812
So what, are we looking
for Waldo here or what?

887
00:33:05,812 --> 00:33:08,068
- [Tom] Anthony! Anthony!

888
00:33:08,068 --> 00:33:09,651
- [Mike] It's Prince Spaghetti Day here

889
00:33:09,651 --> 00:33:12,828
in the Italian north end of the swamp.

890
00:33:12,828 --> 00:33:16,644
- Good morning little flowers,
little flowers on the stump.

891
00:33:16,644 --> 00:33:19,394
- [Crow] Yeah, you got the money?

892
00:33:20,526 --> 00:33:22,608
- [Mike] Oh, well just
make yourself at home.

893
00:33:22,608 --> 00:33:25,132
- Every single day I come to see you.

894
00:33:25,132 --> 00:33:27,343
Every single day I come to talk to you.

895
00:33:27,343 --> 00:33:28,972
I hope that I'm not bothering you.

896
00:33:28,972 --> 00:33:30,236
- [Tom] Have a seat in the waiting room

897
00:33:30,236 --> 00:33:33,145
and one of our flowers will
be with you in a moment.

898
00:33:33,145 --> 00:33:33,978
- It's alright?

899
00:33:33,978 --> 00:33:36,728
- [Crow] ♫ It's okay, Ewing,
I'm in love with you ♫

900
00:33:36,728 --> 00:33:37,872
- Tell me little flowers,

901
00:33:37,872 --> 00:33:40,118
is Ivan still living today?

902
00:33:40,118 --> 00:33:41,301
- [Mike, Tom, Crow] (crosstalk)

903
00:33:41,301 --> 00:33:43,284
- [Tom] Definitely yes, I don't know,

904
00:33:43,284 --> 00:33:44,637
- [Crow] Yeah, you wanna take this?

905
00:33:44,637 --> 00:33:45,769
- He's alive?

906
00:33:45,769 --> 00:33:47,313
- [Crow] We didn't say that.

907
00:33:47,313 --> 00:33:50,725
- He must be angry with me, I suppose.

908
00:33:50,725 --> 00:33:54,812
- [Tom] I need to check with
our flowers on the street.

909
00:33:54,812 --> 00:33:56,465
- You mean he's not?

910
00:33:56,465 --> 00:33:58,273
- [Tom] Hey, I'm just asking
for a straight answer,

911
00:33:58,273 --> 00:34:00,449
don't bust my chops, man.

912
00:34:00,449 --> 00:34:03,059
- Now, tell me, will be ever meet?

913
00:34:03,059 --> 00:34:07,217
- [Crow] Our lawyers have
advised us not to comment.

914
00:34:07,217 --> 00:34:10,134
- [Mike] Ew, what am I kneeling in?

915
00:34:11,168 --> 00:34:15,035
- [Crow] Yes, look for
the answer in the algae.

916
00:34:15,035 --> 00:34:19,859
- [Tom] ♫ From the land
of sky blue waters ♫

917
00:34:19,859 --> 00:34:20,723
- [Ivan] (growling)

918
00:34:20,723 --> 00:34:22,512
- [Tom] I mean where else are you going

919
00:34:22,512 --> 00:34:24,679
to do a butt in the woods?

920
00:34:25,708 --> 00:34:28,362
- [Ivan] Charity dear little
sisters, dear little brothers.

921
00:34:28,362 --> 00:34:31,172
Charity dear little sisters,
dear little brothers.

922
00:34:31,172 --> 00:34:33,705
Charity, give us arms, for without us

923
00:34:33,705 --> 00:34:35,867
you could not prove your charity.

924
00:34:35,867 --> 00:34:37,551
- [Crow] Great, Shakespeare in the Park.

925
00:34:37,551 --> 00:34:41,009
- [Ivan] Give to a poor orphan
who is homeless, penniless,

926
00:34:41,009 --> 00:34:42,551
crippled, and blind.

927
00:34:42,551 --> 00:34:44,319
Give to the poor, the blind, and the deaf.

928
00:34:44,319 --> 00:34:45,709
- [Voiceover] How much
have you in your cup?

929
00:34:45,709 --> 00:34:47,171
- Not a copper, not--

930
00:34:47,171 --> 00:34:48,004
- Ah.

931
00:34:48,004 --> 00:34:50,296
- [Voiceover] If that's
the case, here's a copper.

932
00:34:50,296 --> 00:34:51,829
- [Tom] Now shut up.

933
00:34:51,829 --> 00:34:54,645
- Oh, to do a good deed, I suppose

934
00:34:54,645 --> 00:34:57,062
that one copper isn't enough.

935
00:34:58,242 --> 00:34:59,619
Where are you going?

936
00:34:59,619 --> 00:35:01,032
- [Boy] A werewolf!

937
00:35:01,032 --> 00:35:03,276
(out of breath) run for your lives!

938
00:35:03,276 --> 00:35:05,160
- [Mike] Regain your sight
and grow your leg back.

939
00:35:05,160 --> 00:35:06,326
- [Boy] A werewolf!

940
00:35:06,326 --> 00:35:07,905
- [Crow] A werebear, actually.

941
00:35:07,905 --> 00:35:09,284
- [Boy] A werewolf!

942
00:35:09,284 --> 00:35:12,187
- [Tom] Oh, like you're such a hunk.

943
00:35:12,187 --> 00:35:16,353
- [Ivan] (groaning)
What kind of a good deed

944
00:35:16,353 --> 00:35:17,976
will I have to do?

945
00:35:17,976 --> 00:35:22,050
- [Crow] ♫ What kind of bear am I ♫

946
00:35:22,050 --> 00:35:24,065
- [Mike] Yogurt is not a finger food.

947
00:35:24,065 --> 00:35:25,521
- How sweet.

948
00:35:25,521 --> 00:35:26,539
Naska!

949
00:35:26,539 --> 00:35:28,340
Let's have the braid, quickly.

950
00:35:28,340 --> 00:35:29,717
- [Tom] Beauty consultant, Mrs. Christian.

951
00:35:29,717 --> 00:35:31,258
- Here.

952
00:35:31,258 --> 00:35:33,598
- Mama, why not smear her eyebrows?

953
00:35:33,598 --> 00:35:34,431
- Ah-ha.

954
00:35:35,988 --> 00:35:37,997
- [Crow] Why is she putting
Bisquick on her face?

955
00:35:37,997 --> 00:35:39,158
- [Step-Mother and Marfushka] (laughs)

956
00:35:39,158 --> 00:35:42,727
- [Tom] Why are you so mean
to me, tonta Earnest Borgnine?

957
00:35:42,727 --> 00:35:47,225
- (laughing) Oh, how
lovely you look (laughing).

958
00:35:47,225 --> 00:35:48,213
- [Marfushka] Mama--

959
00:35:48,213 --> 00:35:49,720
- [Tom] Don't let your
babies grow up to be cowboys.

960
00:35:49,720 --> 00:35:51,708
- [Marfushka] Naska's braid
is nicer than mine is.

961
00:35:51,708 --> 00:35:52,632
- [Step-mother] Yours is worth more,

962
00:35:52,632 --> 00:35:54,214
it was bought at the fair.

963
00:35:54,214 --> 00:35:56,111
- I want you to cut off
her braid at the root!

964
00:35:56,111 --> 00:35:57,192
- What could I drag her by

965
00:35:57,192 --> 00:35:58,242
without a braid on her head, I ask.

966
00:35:58,242 --> 00:35:59,448
- [Marfushka] Cut it off!

967
00:35:59,448 --> 00:36:01,534
- I know, I'll put a rag
over her braid to hide it.

968
00:36:01,534 --> 00:36:03,989
- [Marfushka] Alright then, hide it.

969
00:36:03,989 --> 00:36:07,393
- [Crow] Alfalfa's greatest role.

970
00:36:07,393 --> 00:36:10,639
- [Mike] I should have
these caterpillars removed.

971
00:36:10,639 --> 00:36:12,956
- Ah, you munch and guzzle, eh,

972
00:36:12,956 --> 00:36:14,601
it's much easier than working.

973
00:36:14,601 --> 00:36:17,282
- [Crow] Munch and guzzle, what the he--

974
00:36:17,282 --> 00:36:21,224
- There, you see, now you're
dressed for housework.

975
00:36:21,224 --> 00:36:24,200
And now, my darling, you put this on.

976
00:36:24,200 --> 00:36:26,120
- [Tom] It's a Burger King birthday crown.

977
00:36:26,120 --> 00:36:27,597
(Crow laughs).

978
00:36:27,597 --> 00:36:32,482
- Like a princess, darling,
exactly like a princess, yeah?

979
00:36:32,482 --> 00:36:33,870
- Really?

980
00:36:33,870 --> 00:36:35,395
- [Mike] Yeah, I am
pretty hot, aren't I, ugh.

981
00:36:35,395 --> 00:36:38,226
(mother laughing)

982
00:36:38,226 --> 00:36:40,442
- A princess (laughs)

983
00:36:40,442 --> 00:36:42,222
- (laughs) A little red.

984
00:36:42,222 --> 00:36:44,524
- [Crow] And now a bag over
the head completes the look.

985
00:36:44,524 --> 00:36:47,143
- I'm all tired and I'm sweating

986
00:36:47,143 --> 00:36:51,306
- [Tom] It's like having
Andrea Dorkin make you over.

987
00:36:51,306 --> 00:36:52,993
- Nope, not a princess.

988
00:36:52,993 --> 00:36:54,683
- [Tom] She's got that healthy clown glow.

989
00:36:54,683 --> 00:36:55,516
- Oh, no?

990
00:36:57,252 --> 00:36:59,494
- You are a queen,

991
00:36:59,494 --> 00:37:01,179
- [Mike] In that you look
like Freddie Mercury.

992
00:37:01,179 --> 00:37:05,948
- [Crow] She should just
start over from gene one.

993
00:37:05,948 --> 00:37:06,781
- Hmm.

994
00:37:08,584 --> 00:37:11,979
- [Ivan] What kind of good deed can I do?

995
00:37:11,979 --> 00:37:15,559
- [Tom] Maybe negotiate
lasting peace in the mideast?

996
00:37:15,559 --> 00:37:18,210
- [Crow] She's on her way back
from her stick distributor.

997
00:37:18,210 --> 00:37:20,221
- [Tom] Not a very good canoe.

998
00:37:20,221 --> 00:37:22,611
- Ah, I can't walk another step.

999
00:37:22,611 --> 00:37:24,846
- Poor granny, here let me help you.

1000
00:37:24,846 --> 00:37:28,352
- Yes, my boy, help me and
it will be a good deed.

1001
00:37:28,352 --> 00:37:31,471
- [Ivan] It would be a good
deed, oh, I'd be glad to help.

1002
00:37:31,471 --> 00:37:32,770
I need to do a good deed.

1003
00:37:32,770 --> 00:37:33,603
- Good boy.

1004
00:37:33,603 --> 00:37:35,111
- I need to very badly.

1005
00:37:35,111 --> 00:37:35,944
Get on.

1006
00:37:35,944 --> 00:37:37,327
- What do I get on?

1007
00:37:37,327 --> 00:37:38,319
- [Ivan] On my back.

1008
00:37:38,319 --> 00:37:39,326
- On your back?

1009
00:37:39,326 --> 00:37:40,276
(laughing)

1010
00:37:40,276 --> 00:37:41,109
- Hang on.

1011
00:37:41,109 --> 00:37:42,550
- [Mike] It's like bear transit.

1012
00:37:42,550 --> 00:37:44,194
- [Ivan] Do you live
far from here, Granny?

1013
00:37:44,194 --> 00:37:46,980
- [Granny] Oh yes, very,
very far just up the mountain

1014
00:37:46,980 --> 00:37:50,018
and down again and up the
mountain on the other side.

1015
00:37:50,018 --> 00:37:52,250
- [Ivan] Hey, that sounds very good.

1016
00:37:52,250 --> 00:37:53,992
[Granny] Well if you
think so, that's fine,

1017
00:37:53,992 --> 00:37:55,338
but don't get all in a sweat.

1018
00:37:55,338 --> 00:37:56,171
- [Ivan] Go?

1019
00:37:56,171 --> 00:37:57,004
- [Granny] Giddy up, let's go.

1020
00:37:57,004 --> 00:37:58,361
Let me tell you...

1021
00:37:58,361 --> 00:37:59,194
- [Tom] Babe!

1022
00:37:59,194 --> 00:38:02,147
- [Tom, Mike, Crow] Oh
no, babe (pretend crying).

1023
00:38:02,147 --> 00:38:04,112
- Works day and night, sews
and knits all the time except

1024
00:38:04,112 --> 00:38:06,986
in the morning when
she gulps down her tea.

1025
00:38:06,986 --> 00:38:08,599
Lights the fire and gets the breakfast.

1026
00:38:08,599 --> 00:38:10,194
Then she mops the floor and then,

1027
00:38:10,194 --> 00:38:12,050
when the breakfast is ready, she--

1028
00:38:12,050 --> 00:38:15,625
- I tell you she's a marvel,
she's perfect in ever respect.

1029
00:38:15,625 --> 00:38:17,923
And no dream princess could be lovelier.

1030
00:38:17,923 --> 00:38:18,771
(two women laughing)

1031
00:38:18,771 --> 00:38:20,644
- [Mike] And she's
available for sale or lease.

1032
00:38:20,644 --> 00:38:21,477
(hits wooden spoon on table)

1033
00:38:21,477 --> 00:38:24,041
- This matchmaker can certainly talk.

1034
00:38:24,041 --> 00:38:26,285
I think there was
something else we wanted.

1035
00:38:26,285 --> 00:38:27,463
- Yes.

1036
00:38:27,463 --> 00:38:29,517
- We hear you have another daughter.

1037
00:38:29,517 --> 00:38:30,350
- Uh.

1038
00:38:30,350 --> 00:38:32,580
- Good lord, people say
the craziest things.

1039
00:38:32,580 --> 00:38:35,784
I am Mama's only daughter,
the other one's not my sister.

1040
00:38:35,784 --> 00:38:37,985
- That's alright, we'll have
a look at the other one,

1041
00:38:37,985 --> 00:38:39,504
if you don't mind.

1042
00:38:39,504 --> 00:38:40,337
- Mama.

1043
00:38:40,337 --> 00:38:41,673
- [Crow] Uh-oh, there's a ripple

1044
00:38:41,673 --> 00:38:43,515
in the daughter market today.

1045
00:38:43,515 --> 00:38:45,196
- Well, alright.

1046
00:38:45,196 --> 00:38:47,752
- You'll see her since you insist.

1047
00:38:47,752 --> 00:38:51,668
Nastenka, Nastenka,

1048
00:38:51,668 --> 00:38:53,103
Nastenka

1049
00:38:53,103 --> 00:38:54,927
- [Tom] Quick, put the dog in a dress!

1050
00:38:54,927 --> 00:38:57,910
- Nashka,

1051
00:38:57,910 --> 00:38:59,470
come here.

1052
00:38:59,470 --> 00:39:00,502
- [Mike] Well, thanks for listening,

1053
00:39:00,502 --> 00:39:02,669
just my fleas got me down.

1054
00:39:04,041 --> 00:39:05,314
- (growl) Get in there you little viper.

1055
00:39:05,314 --> 00:39:08,658
- [Crow] Somebody needs viping.

1056
00:39:08,658 --> 00:39:13,279
- Nastenka, sweet heart
of mine, my honey child.

1057
00:39:13,279 --> 00:39:16,665
Come let these folks look at you.

1058
00:39:16,665 --> 00:39:17,925
- [Crow] Larry Drake and Vanessa Redgrave.

1059
00:39:17,925 --> 00:39:19,105
- Um-hmm.

1060
00:39:19,105 --> 00:39:22,438
No matchmaker, this one won't do it all.

1061
00:39:23,306 --> 00:39:25,556
She looks like a scarecrow.

1062
00:39:26,792 --> 00:39:29,391
- [Mike] Now get out there and
do something Russo-Finnish.

1063
00:39:29,391 --> 00:39:32,392
- Yes, our little idiot is
really horrible looking.

1064
00:39:32,392 --> 00:39:33,364
- [Crow] Geez (laughs)

1065
00:39:33,364 --> 00:39:34,567
- Image of her father.

1066
00:39:34,567 --> 00:39:35,400
- I'll--

1067
00:39:35,400 --> 00:39:36,233
(Stepmother huffs)

1068
00:39:36,233 --> 00:39:38,070
I won't say it, I'll be quiet.

1069
00:39:38,070 --> 00:39:39,556
- [Crow] Cabbage burp (fake burp).

1070
00:39:39,556 --> 00:39:42,783
- Alright, now start the
feast, my dear guests.

1071
00:39:42,783 --> 00:39:45,998
- That's what I've been waiting
for, I drink to your health.

1072
00:39:45,998 --> 00:39:46,831
- [Woman In Light Blue) That's very well,

1073
00:39:46,831 --> 00:39:49,530
but my son likes goose giblets,
that's his favorite dish.

1074
00:39:49,530 --> 00:39:50,669
- Ah, yes.

1075
00:39:50,669 --> 00:39:52,514
- [Crow] Ah, Andy (indiscernible).

1076
00:39:52,514 --> 00:39:53,347
Nastka?

1077
00:39:53,347 --> 00:39:54,709
- [Woman in Light Blue] Ah,
no, your lovely daughter

1078
00:39:54,709 --> 00:39:56,942
should take care of it, it's up to her.

1079
00:39:56,942 --> 00:39:58,025
That's the custom you know.

1080
00:39:58,025 --> 00:39:59,109
- Mama.

1081
00:39:59,109 --> 00:40:00,551
- [Woman In Light Blue] That
way my son and I can see

1082
00:40:00,551 --> 00:40:02,284
what kind of a bride we're getting.

1083
00:40:02,284 --> 00:40:03,919
- [Crow] Some day I'll be a real boy.

1084
00:40:03,919 --> 00:40:04,894
- [Marfushka] Hm.

1085
00:40:04,894 --> 00:40:07,727
(high-tech music)

1086
00:40:11,078 --> 00:40:12,133
- Well, Tom, I suppose
we should to check in

1087
00:40:12,133 --> 00:40:14,916
with those two and see--
- Little problem here, guys.

1088
00:40:14,916 --> 00:40:15,749
I'm a bear.

1089
00:40:15,749 --> 00:40:17,219
- [Tom] Oh, I'm so sure.

1090
00:40:17,219 --> 00:40:18,345
- Yep, I'm a bear.

1091
00:40:18,345 --> 00:40:21,925
That little, uh, you know,
that-that Mushroom head elf guy?

1092
00:40:21,925 --> 00:40:22,783
- [Mike] Uh-huh.
- You know?

1093
00:40:22,783 --> 00:40:24,357
- [Mike] Yeah.
- He did it.

1094
00:40:24,357 --> 00:40:27,222
- Oh, huh, and uh, where did this happen?

1095
00:40:27,222 --> 00:40:29,487
- Just, you know, around.

1096
00:40:29,487 --> 00:40:31,505
Shh, some luck, huh?

1097
00:40:31,505 --> 00:40:32,338
- [Mike] Yeah.

1098
00:40:32,338 --> 00:40:34,890
You sure you didn't just hot
glue some fur to yourself?

1099
00:40:34,890 --> 00:40:36,057
- Hey, I wish.

1100
00:40:37,523 --> 00:40:39,720
- (laughs) Yeah, well, huh, a bear.

1101
00:40:39,720 --> 00:40:41,595
Well, we better check in with these two,

1102
00:40:41,595 --> 00:40:43,053
see how the peace process is going.

1103
00:40:43,053 --> 00:40:45,372
- [Tom] Bear, huh, what a feeb.

1104
00:40:45,372 --> 00:40:46,205
- Grr.

1105
00:40:47,405 --> 00:40:50,072
(slurping food)

1106
00:40:54,674 --> 00:40:55,674
- Oh, sorry.

1107
00:41:00,021 --> 00:41:01,829
- Well, thank you

1108
00:41:01,829 --> 00:41:05,836
Oh you're welcome, and thank
you for laundering your cape.

1109
00:41:05,836 --> 00:41:08,488
- Oh well, think nothing of it.

1110
00:41:08,488 --> 00:41:12,437
- Ah, yeah, would you
like some mashed banana?

1111
00:41:12,437 --> 00:41:13,683
- Uh, no no no no no

1112
00:41:13,683 --> 00:41:15,193
- Oh, you're sure about that?

1113
00:41:15,193 --> 00:41:16,932
It's nice and rotten, ah.

1114
00:41:16,932 --> 00:41:18,983
I don't eat it 'til the
fruit flies come a'buzzin'.

1115
00:41:18,983 --> 00:41:20,246
That's good eatin'.

1116
00:41:20,246 --> 00:41:22,343
- I'm sure that it is, but--

1117
00:41:22,343 --> 00:41:23,406
yum.

1118
00:41:23,406 --> 00:41:26,656
- (laughs) Yeah, yeah.

1119
00:41:29,851 --> 00:41:32,278
So, what are you up to?

1120
00:41:32,278 --> 00:41:35,044
- Oh, I'm reading the
entire galactic library

1121
00:41:35,044 --> 00:41:38,841
of the Venuzian eight
system at once with my mind.

1122
00:41:38,841 --> 00:41:40,044
- Ah, oh, nice.

1123
00:41:40,044 --> 00:41:41,268
- Yes.

1124
00:41:41,268 --> 00:41:42,498
- Are there pictures?

1125
00:41:42,498 --> 00:41:44,775
- Ah, several trillion, yes.

1126
00:41:44,775 --> 00:41:47,927
- Oh (laughs).

1127
00:41:47,927 --> 00:41:50,552
Oh say, my toe's feeling better. (laughs)

1128
00:41:50,552 --> 00:41:53,068
Most of the seep had just dried up.

1129
00:41:53,068 --> 00:41:55,851
- Well, uh, hallelujah (laughs).

1130
00:41:55,851 --> 00:41:59,184
(crows caw in distance)

1131
00:42:00,490 --> 00:42:02,239
(whistles)

1132
00:42:02,239 --> 00:42:04,064
- Do you

1133
00:42:04,064 --> 00:42:05,663
do you find that uh,

1134
00:42:05,663 --> 00:42:09,271
oh, that the law giver can be

1135
00:42:09,271 --> 00:42:10,521
mean sometimes?

1136
00:42:11,669 --> 00:42:14,240
- Well, it's against my
culture to gossip, I--

1137
00:42:14,240 --> 00:42:16,073
- oh sure, but do you?

1138
00:42:17,963 --> 00:42:21,710
- Yes, she can really be a
stone cold witch some times.

1139
00:42:21,710 --> 00:42:24,103
- I know and she can be so condescending.

1140
00:42:24,103 --> 00:42:25,429
- Oh, precisely, it's
like oh, I'm so great

1141
00:42:25,429 --> 00:42:26,510
and I don't have--

1142
00:42:26,510 --> 00:42:27,984
- Oh, would you look at that, looks like

1143
00:42:27,984 --> 00:42:29,560
those two finally found
something in common.

1144
00:42:29,560 --> 00:42:30,560
- Mike help!

1145
00:42:31,982 --> 00:42:34,509
- Oh ate half of me and
then buried me in the dirt.

1146
00:42:34,509 --> 00:42:35,447
- [Tom] Oh, not bad.

1147
00:42:35,447 --> 00:42:36,878
- Crow, what is wrong with you?

1148
00:42:36,878 --> 00:42:38,657
- What, I told you Mike, I'm a bear.

1149
00:42:38,657 --> 00:42:40,706
- Now haven't we talked
about this a hundred times,

1150
00:42:40,706 --> 00:42:43,784
about you taking your bear
simulations to the extreme?

1151
00:42:43,784 --> 00:42:44,691
- Uh, yeah.

1152
00:42:44,691 --> 00:42:46,343
- Uh-hih, and what are you doing?

1153
00:42:46,343 --> 00:42:48,784
- Uh, taking my bear
simulation to the extreme?

1154
00:42:48,784 --> 00:42:50,385
- There, now do you see the connection?

1155
00:42:50,385 --> 00:42:51,758
- Mm, no.

1156
00:42:51,758 --> 00:42:54,111
- Oh, Okay well let me explain,
see when you're a bear--

1157
00:42:54,111 --> 00:42:55,077
(alarm)

1158
00:42:55,077 --> 00:42:58,432
we've got movie, I'll explain later!

1159
00:42:58,432 --> 00:42:59,872
(doors loudly open)

1160
00:42:59,872 --> 00:43:01,719
(squeaking metal door shutting)

1161
00:43:01,719 --> 00:43:02,694
(door slamming)

1162
00:43:02,694 --> 00:43:04,002
(computer beep)

1163
00:43:04,002 --> 00:43:05,053
(metal door slamming)

1164
00:43:05,053 --> 00:43:06,619
(computer beep)

1165
00:43:06,619 --> 00:43:07,452
(metal door sliding)

1166
00:43:07,452 --> 00:43:08,494
(squeaking metal)

1167
00:43:08,494 --> 00:43:09,863
(metal door slamming)

1168
00:43:09,863 --> 00:43:11,662
- [Crow] Just gonna have to
get used to me as a bear.

1169
00:43:11,662 --> 00:43:14,641
- And your on your way, dear boy.

1170
00:43:14,641 --> 00:43:16,131
- It's really hot.

1171
00:43:16,131 --> 00:43:18,646
- And can you see some old
tumbled down houses yet?

1172
00:43:18,646 --> 00:43:19,689
- I see them.

1173
00:43:19,689 --> 00:43:20,822
- Well, they're my castles boy

1174
00:43:20,822 --> 00:43:21,655
- [Crow] Grr.

1175
00:43:21,655 --> 00:43:22,928
- Yes. Faster.

1176
00:43:22,928 --> 00:43:25,335
Come on, hurry, hurry,
or you'll catch cold.

1177
00:43:25,335 --> 00:43:27,556
Can't you feel it, that
cold mountain wind.

1178
00:43:27,556 --> 00:43:28,905
Come on, faster, faster.

1179
00:43:28,905 --> 00:43:30,411
- [Mike] Forget the good deed, eat her!

1180
00:43:30,411 --> 00:43:31,597
(Ivan groans)

1181
00:43:31,597 --> 00:43:33,847
- [Grandmother] Here we
are, we're home at last.

1182
00:43:33,847 --> 00:43:37,583
Yes at last we're home
and my home is my castle.

1183
00:43:37,583 --> 00:43:39,677
I'm much obliged to
you my handsome prince.

1184
00:43:39,677 --> 00:43:40,728
- Huh?

1185
00:43:40,728 --> 00:43:41,914
- [Tom] Most bears don't carry compacts.

1186
00:43:41,914 --> 00:43:42,747
- [Crow] True.
- Look, granny,

1187
00:43:42,747 --> 00:43:43,990
are you making fun of me?

1188
00:43:43,990 --> 00:43:44,823
- Of course not.

1189
00:43:44,823 --> 00:43:46,586
- [Ivan] Look at me before
you call me handsome.

1190
00:43:46,586 --> 00:43:49,721
- I can't very well do that
boy, it's been at least...

1191
00:43:49,721 --> 00:43:52,955
yes, it's been ten years since
I last looked at something.

1192
00:43:52,955 --> 00:43:55,281
You see, I'm blind.

1193
00:43:55,281 --> 00:43:57,931
- [Ivan] Oh grandma I wish I
could've gone blind for you.

1194
00:43:57,931 --> 00:43:59,826
- Oh no, how you talk.

1195
00:43:59,826 --> 00:44:01,953
Father Mushroom lied.

1196
00:44:01,953 --> 00:44:03,167
- Who did?

1197
00:44:03,167 --> 00:44:05,733
- And I'll never look at myself again.

1198
00:44:05,733 --> 00:44:06,566
(crash)

1199
00:44:06,566 --> 00:44:08,370
- [Crow] Oh, blame the mirror.

1200
00:44:08,370 --> 00:44:10,322
(ducks quacking)

1201
00:44:10,322 --> 00:44:12,738
- [Mike] Invasion of
the the matruska people.

1202
00:44:12,738 --> 00:44:14,395
(geese quack)

1203
00:44:14,395 --> 00:44:15,420
- What do you say, son?

1204
00:44:15,420 --> 00:44:16,253
- [Ivan] Uh.

1205
00:44:16,253 --> 00:44:17,639
- Let me talk, he likes her very much.

1206
00:44:17,639 --> 00:44:20,278
Anybody can see she's lovely, such beauty,

1207
00:44:20,278 --> 00:44:22,426
she's in perfect health,
I tell you, all over.

1208
00:44:22,426 --> 00:44:23,912
(geese quack)

1209
00:44:23,912 --> 00:44:25,494
- [Tom] She's imprinting on the geese.

1210
00:44:25,494 --> 00:44:27,002
- [Women] Oh, hurry!

1211
00:44:27,002 --> 00:44:31,148
- [Crow] (laughs) and
the freelance shame squad

1212
00:44:31,148 --> 00:44:31,981
is there.

1213
00:44:31,981 --> 00:44:33,714
(Crowd laughing and geese quacking)

1214
00:44:33,714 --> 00:44:35,184
- [Tom] Oh, the pond
scum is fleeing in terror

1215
00:44:35,184 --> 00:44:36,228
from her face.

1216
00:44:36,228 --> 00:44:38,067
- [Mother] Marfushka, my darling daughter.

1217
00:44:38,067 --> 00:44:39,148
- [Marfushka] Help!

1218
00:44:39,148 --> 00:44:40,621
(ducks quacking)

1219
00:44:40,621 --> 00:44:42,220
- Mama

1220
00:44:42,220 --> 00:44:44,715
- [Tom] People's distress is funny.

1221
00:44:44,715 --> 00:44:45,548
- Oh, don't say--

1222
00:44:45,548 --> 00:44:47,105
- [Tom] She caught a water moccasin.

1223
00:44:47,105 --> 00:44:48,842
- [Nastenka] Oh, Marfushka!

1224
00:44:48,842 --> 00:44:50,068
- [Mother] my daughter, my daughter!

1225
00:44:50,068 --> 00:44:51,231
(crowd laughing)

1226
00:44:51,231 --> 00:44:53,987
- [Crow] , well, I guess you
have to be Russo-Finnish to--

1227
00:44:53,987 --> 00:44:54,841
(Mike laughs)

1228
00:44:54,841 --> 00:44:56,424
- [Marfushka] Mama!

1229
00:44:58,849 --> 00:45:01,720
- Look my dear, maybe you
should've tied it tighter.

1230
00:45:01,720 --> 00:45:03,170
- [Mother] Forget my daughter, then.

1231
00:45:03,170 --> 00:45:05,869
Oh my sweet little gem.

1232
00:45:05,869 --> 00:45:06,702
- What?

1233
00:45:06,702 --> 00:45:09,823
There's no telling what
bride a boy will take.

1234
00:45:09,823 --> 00:45:11,631
And my son's not stupid.

1235
00:45:11,631 --> 00:45:13,944
He's ready to take a wife.

1236
00:45:13,944 --> 00:45:15,199
Aren't you?

1237
00:45:15,199 --> 00:45:16,199
- [Tom] Duh.

1238
00:45:17,371 --> 00:45:19,087
(crying loudly)

1239
